// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6626 new: Suspicious Renamed MSBuild Execution
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6626
// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Renamed MSBuild Execution
// Sigma ID: 0df03709-f088-49fd-b668-3934e8b8b8e3
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-11-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1036.003, T1127.001
// Description: Detects the execution of the Microsoft Build Engine ("MSBuild.exe" according to its
//   OriginalFileName) from an image that does not carry the MSBuild file name. MSBuild compiles and
//   runs inline C# or VB tasks from a project file and is a well-known application control bypass;
//   renaming the binary is done to evade detections that key on the process name while keeping the
//   trusted Microsoft signature.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Msbuild/
//   - https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/f4ef34b1c996da53880053dd497ca546c1b0bbfa/rules/windows/defense_evasion_execution_msbuild_started_renamed.toml
//   - https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/93290/
//   - https://lab52.io/blog/plugx-meeting-invitation-via-msbuild-and-gdata/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/5b5f3371caf1b460acf58b6765ddb97f6a2ccddd/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_msbuild.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "MSBuild.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\MSBuild.exe"))
